<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74624" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁπόστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>in
				what</i> or <i>which place in numerical order,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁπόστον μέρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Archyt.
					1
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. εἰλήχει</span>
			<i>what number</i> he had drawn, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				617e
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. ἐγένετο ἀφ᾽ Ἡρακλέους</span>
			<i>how many generations</i> from . . , <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Ages.</u>
				1.2
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὕτως ὁπόστος τὸν ἀριθμόν,
				κτλ.,</span> in a sense determined by <i>the number of which
				he is one,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1262a3
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ πρῶτος, οὐ δεύτερος . . , οὐχ
					ὁποστοσοῦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.310
				</span></i>
			.</div>
